Subject: [PATCH] logging: snapshot canonical validation diagnostics without
 caller formatting

Add non-owning GetRejectReasonView/GetDebugMessageView accessors while preserving the existing owning getters, ToString, member layout and every validation decision. Pack TxValidationState/BlockValidationState mode and bounded string bytes into typed records; reconstruct the exact canonical diagnostic on the consumer. Oversize states are omitted with fields_truncated instead of a partial reason or overflow. No production callers converted here.

Manually authored adapter feature, not a scripted call conversion. Fifteen artifact ASan/UBSan snapshot/mode/NUL/saturation checks pass. Native tests cover both state types, post-pack mutation, actual JSON fields, oversize omission and size saturation. Full logger allocation controls compare original ToString arguments with typed snapshots against the same consistently rebuilt candidate; report calibrated caller allocations and actual callback records, not sink throughput. Controls run before the functional suite, not concurrently with it.

Allocation control results: [('before', [256, 256, 256], True), ('after', [0, 0, 0], True)].
All five targets and focused native suites pass; full STANDARD {'total': 320, 'failed': 0, 'errors': 0, 'skipped': 61, 'passed': 259}. Frozen tree 7be19ac5e399fef530c89edd58105cd04da46778. No extended gate.

